%SIXMD 1
# @?DARC - CREATE A DOBJ ARCHIVE

## DESCRIPTION

DARC CREATES A DARC1 ARCHIVE FROM ONE OR MORE DOBJ1 OBJECT FILES. THE ARCHIVE
INDEX MAPS EACH DEFINED GLOBAL SYMBOL TO THE MEMBER WHICH PROVIDES IT, SO
DLINK CAN LOAD MEMBERS ON DEMAND.

USAGE IS 'DARC -O ARCHIVE.DARC OBJECT.DOBJ ...'.

THE NATIVE DAIMOS IMPLEMENTATION IS BOUNDED AND STREAMING. IT ACCEPTS AT MOST
16 INPUT OBJECTS IN ONE INVOCATION AND DOES NOT MATERIALIZE OBJECT TEXT OR
DATA IN PROCESS MEMORY.

## @?OPTIONS

### @?-O ARCHIVE.DARC
WRITE THE RESULTING DARC1 ARCHIVE.

## @?OPERANDS

### @?OBJECT.DOBJ
DOBJ1 OBJECT TO ADD TO THE ARCHIVE.

## @?EXIT STATUS

### @?0 - ARCHIVE CREATED
### @?1 - INVALID INPUT, LIMIT, OR FILE ERROR

